CONTEXT Migration INCLUDES Garden FROM "existing.adl" AS old,
                           Garden FROM "desired.adl" AS new
CONTEXT Migration IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Migration
{+ The migration of the plot register of the community garden to its new release.
The register in use is included as `old`, the new release as `new`.
The gardeners keep working while the data moves, and they find keepers for the plots that have none. +}

-- Every plot, name and gardener of the register in use is one of the new release.
CLASSIFY old.Plot ISA new.Plot
CLASSIFY old.PlotName ISA new.PlotName
CLASSIFY old.Gardener ISA new.Gardener

-- Copy the names and the keepers. The relations copyName and copyKeeper register what has been copied,
-- so that a change that a user makes in the new release is not undone by the copy.
RELATION copyName[old.Plot*old.PlotName]
ENFORCE copyNameDone : copyName >: new.name /\ old.name
ENFORCE copyTheName : new.name >: old.name - copyName
RELATION copyKeeper[old.Plot*old.Gardener]
ENFORCE copyKeeperDone : copyKeeper >: new.keeper /\ old.keeper
ENFORCE copyTheKeeper : new.keeper >: old.keeper - copyKeeper

-- The new rule of the board: every plot has a keeper. Plots without a keeper come along from the register in use,
-- so the migration system relaxes the rule, with steps 3 to 5 of the migration method.
-- Step 3: the relation fixedEveryPlotHasKeeper holds the plots that have a keeper,
-- and the blocking invariant blockEveryPlotHasKeeper keeps such a plot from losing it again.
RELATION fixedEveryPlotHasKeeper[new.Plot*new.Plot]
RULE blockEveryPlotHasKeeper : fixedEveryPlotHasKeeper |- new.keeper;new.keeper~
MESSAGE "A plot that has a keeper keeps one."
VIOLATION (TXT "Give ", SRC new.name, TXT " a keeper again.")
-- Step 4: a transactional invariant registers every plot that has a keeper.
ENFORCE fixEveryPlotHasKeeper : fixedEveryPlotHasKeeper >: I[new.Plot] /\ new.keeper;new.keeper~
-- Step 5: the rule itself signals the plots without a keeper, as work for the volunteers.
-- In the new release, where no role maintains it, the same rule is a blocking invariant.
ROLE Volunteer MAINTAINS new.everyPlotHasKeeper

-- The screens of the new release, so that a user of the migration system works as in the new release:
-- a list that cannot be edited, and a screen for one plot that saves a change as one transaction.
INTERFACE Plots FOR Volunteer : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*new.Plot] cRud BOX<TABLE showNavMenu>
  [ "plot" : new.name cRud
  , "keeper" : new.keeper cRud
  ]

TRANSACTIONAL INTERFACE Plot FOR Volunteer : I[new.Plot] CRuD BOX<FORM>
  [ "plot" : new.name CRUD
  , "keeper" : new.keeper CRUD
  ]

ENDCONTEXT
